  <h2>Specification</h2>
  <p>The SDBM algorithm provides a good general purpose hash function with a fairly even distribution across the 32 bit space in the general case.
The characters fed into the hash function are 32bit wide.</p>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`U32 SDBMHash(const std::wstring &val)
{
    U32 hash(0);

    for(const wchar_t &c: val)
    {
        hash = c + (hash << 6) + (hash << 16) - hash;
    }
    return hash;
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>In LSL:</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

local function llSDBMHash(value)
    local hash = 0
    local index = 0
    index = 0
    while index < ll.StringLength(value) do
        hash = ll.Ord(value, index) + bit32.lshift(hash, 6) + bit32.lshift(hash, 16) - hash
        index += 1
    end

    return hash
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`integer llSDBMHash(string value)
{
    integer hash = 0;
    integer index = 0;
    for (index = 0; index < llStringLength(value); ++index)
    {
        hash = llOrd(value, index) + (hash << 6) + (hash << 16) - hash;
    }
    
    return hash;
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <p>This hash value is not cryptographically secure and should not be used as part of any security protocol.
SDBM provides a good distribution of hash values across its range, however with only
32 bits the chance of a collision is unacceptably high.(with 1000 entries, the odds for a collision are about 1 in 10000.)</p>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
  <p>Given the combination of the object name and the owner&#39;s key generate a unique number. This number could be used for things
like selecting a chat channel that has a low probability of colliding with another object.</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local function pickIDForObject()
    --[[ Generate an arbitrary integer ID for the combination of the
     * object name and the ower's key.  This value could be used 
     * for selecting a chat/listen channel. 
     ]]
    local obj_name = ll.GetObjectName()
    local obj_owner = ll.GetOwner()

    local hash = ll.Hash(obj_name .. tostring(obj_owner))

    return hash
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`integer pickIDForObject()
{
    /* Generate an arbitrary integer ID for the combination of the
     * object name and the ower's key.  This value could be used 
     * for selecting a chat/listen channel. 
     */
    string obj_name = llGetObjectName();
    key obj_owner = llGetOwner();
    
    integer hash = llHash(obj_name + (string)obj_owner);
    
    return hash;
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
